    <item>
      <title>Solved: How to Fix &#39;asyncio.run cannot be called from a running event loop&#39; Error in Jupyter Notebook</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-asyncio-run-cannot-be-called-from-a-running-event-loop-error-in-jupyter-notebook/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 05 Dec 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-fix-asyncio-run-cannot-be-called-from-a-running-event-loop-error-in-jupyter-notebook/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;When working with Jupyter Notebook, you might encounter the &lt;strong&gt;RuntimeError&lt;/strong&gt; stating that &lt;strong&gt;&lt;code&gt;asyncio.run()&lt;/code&gt; cannot be called from a running event loop&lt;/strong&gt;. This can be frustrating, especially when you aim to utilize the power of asyncio for asynchronous programming. Let’s delve into this issue comprehensively and offer effective solutions to take care of this common predicament.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem-analysis&#34;&gt;Problem Analysis&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;You might be trying to execute the following code:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; aiofiles&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; aiohttp&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; aiohttp &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; ClientSession&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;fetch_info&lt;/span&gt;(url, session):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    response &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; session&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;request(method&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;GET&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, url&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;url)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    response&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;raise_for_status()&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    html &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; response&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;text(encoding&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;utf-8&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;with&lt;/span&gt; open(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;output.html&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;w&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, encoding&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;utf-8-sig&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; file:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        file&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;write(html)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; html&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;def&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#a6e22e&#34;&gt;main&lt;/span&gt;(urls):&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;async&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;with&lt;/span&gt; ClientSession() &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;as&lt;/span&gt; session:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        tasks &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; [fetch_info(url, session) &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; url &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; urls]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;return&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;await&lt;/span&gt; asyncio&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;gather(&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt;tasks)&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; __name__ &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;==&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;__main__&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;:&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    url_list &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; [&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;http://example.com/page1&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;http://example.com/page2&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    result &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; asyncio&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;run(main(url_list))&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Upon execution, this code results in a &lt;strong&gt;RuntimeError&lt;/strong&gt;. This occurs because Jupyter Notebook operates on a running event loop, and &lt;code&gt;asyncio.run()&lt;/code&gt; tries to start a new loop.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solved: How to Implement &#39;Fire and Forget&#39; in Python Async/Await</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-implement-fire-and-forget-in-python-async-await/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 06 Nov 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/solved-how-to-implement-fire-and-forget-in-python-async-await/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Sometimes, you may encounter situations in Python where you need to perform non-critical asynchronous tasks without holding up the flow of your application. With the release of Python 3.5, the &lt;code&gt;async&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;await&lt;/code&gt; keywords introduced a more structured way to handle asynchronous operations. However, the challenge arises when you want to &amp;ldquo;fire and forget&amp;rdquo; an asynchronous function without awaiting its completion.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;exploring-the-fire-and-forget-concept&#34;&gt;Exploring the &amp;ldquo;Fire and Forget&amp;rdquo; Concept&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let’s dive deeper into how you can achieve this functionality in Python.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Top 5 Methods to Perform Asynchronous HTTP Requests in Python with Asyncio</title>
